Project Supporting Women’s Political Participation in North Kivu Province (Micro-project)

**Location:** Goma City, North Kivu Province (DRC)\
**Period:** April 2021 (1 month)\
**Partner:** CARE International\
**Program:** Gender Equality Women’s Empowerment Program (GEWEP 3)\
**Funders:** NORAD and Telethon

In North Kivu Province, women remain underrepresented in political decision-making spaces despite their active engagement in their communities. Removing the barriers to their participation is essential to building more inclusive and equitable governance.

Carried out in April 2021 in Goma, this micro-project was part of CARE International’s GEWEP 3 program, with support from NORAD and Telethon. It aimed to:

- **Encourage** women’s participation in political life and decision-making processes;
- **Raise awareness** within communities of the importance of women’s leadership;
- **Build women’s confidence and skills** to engage in political action;
- **Contribute to gender equality** and women’s empowerment.

Though short in duration, this initiative helped promote greater involvement of women in local political life.
